      <div type="clause" n="65">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 65</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa burhbote oððe brycgbote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.7-2"/> oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.8-2"/> scyll' þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.9-2"/> on Engla lage, ⁊ on Dena lage swa hit ær stod; oððe geladige hine: namie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.10"/> man him XIIII, ⁊ begyte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.11"/> XI.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Burhbote. Gyf hwa buruhbote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.1"/> oððe brycebote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.2"/> oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid hundtwentigum scill' ðam kyncge on Engle lage, ⁊ on Dena lage swa hit ær stod; oððe geladige <hi rend="italic">hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.3"/></hi>, ⁊ namige man him XIIII, ⁊ begyte XI [þærtó<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.4"/>].</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa burhbote oððe bricgbote oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid hundtwel[f]tigu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.2-2"/></hi> scill' þam cyninge on Engla lage, ⁊ on Dena lage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.3-2"/> swa hit ær stod; oððe geladige <hi rend="italic">hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.4-2"/></hi>: namige him man XIIII, ⁊ begyte XI.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis burhbotam uel brigbotam (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.14"/> est burgi uel pontis emendationem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.15"/> [refectionem]) uel fyrdfare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.16"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.14"/> est in exercitum ire) supersederit; emendet hoc erga regem CXX solidis in Anglorum laga, in Denalaga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.17"/> sicut stetit antea; uel ita se adlegiet: nominentur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.18"/> ei XIIII, et adquirat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.19"/> ex eis XI.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis neglexerit emendationem ciuitatis uel pontis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.6"/> aut ire ad bellum, soluat regi XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.7-3"/> solidos; aut ita sé purget: nominentur ei quattuordecim, et adquirat undecim et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.8-3"/> ipse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_65.lnote.oe.9-3"/> sit duodecimus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="65" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis urbis refectionem siue pontis refectionem siue exercitus it[in]eracionem neglexerit, soluat regi CXX solidos in lege Anglorum, et in lege Danorum sicut prius institutum fuit; aut se purget sic: annominentur illi XIIII, et perquirat X[I].</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="65" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="206" ed="#robertson"/>Burhbote. Gyf hwa buruhbote oððe brygcebote<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_65.robnote.fn.1"/> oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid hundtwentigum<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_65.robnote.fn.2"/> scill' ðam kyncge on Engle lage, ⁊ on Dena lage swa hit ær stod, oððe geladige hine, (⁊)<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_65.robnote.fn.3"/> namige man him XIIII ⁊ begyte XI<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_65.robnote.fn.4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa burhbote oððe brycgbote oððe fyrdfare forsitte, gebete mid CXX scyllingum þam cingce on Engla lage, and on Dena lage swa hit ær stod, oððe geladige hine: namie man him XIIII, and begyte XI.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>(Burgbesserung. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>). Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_65.lnote.de.1"/> einer Burgherstellung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_65.lnote.de.2"/> oder Brückenherrichtung oder Landwehrfahrt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_65.lnote.de.3"/> versäumt, büsse er dem König nach Engländer-Recht mit 120 Schill., und im Dänen-Recht wie es bisher galt; oder er schwöre sich rein: [das Gericht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_65.lnote.de.4"/>] ernenne ihm 14, und er gewinne 11 [davon sich zu Eideshelfern].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Repair of fortifications. B) If anyone neglects the repair of fortifications or the making-ready of bridges or service in the army, let him atone to the king under English law with 120 shillings, and under Danish law as it has held hitherto; or let him clear himself by oath: let [the court] name 14 for him, and let him win 11 [of them as his oath-helpers].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="207" ed="#robertson"/>The repair of fortifications. If anyone neglects the repair of fortifications or of bridges or military service<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_65.robnote.n.1"/>, he shall pay 120 shillings as compensation to the king in districts under English law, and in the Danelaw the amount fixed by existing regulations; or he shall clear himself—[the court] shall nominate 14 compurgators for him and he shall obtain the support of 11 of them.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="471" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone neglects the repair of fortresses or bridges, or military service, he is to pay 120 shillings compensation to the king in the area under English law, and in the Danelaw as it stood before; or to clear himself; fourteen men are to be nominated to him, and he is to get [the support of] eleven.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="287" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone neglects the upkeep of fortifications, the repair of bridges, or required military service, he is to pay one hundred twenty shillings to the king in areas under English law, and under the Danelaw as it was previously decreed, unless he exonerates himself: fourteen potential witnesses shall be identified for him, of which he must obtain the support of eleven.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_14-1">Leis Wl 14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann prints G as ‘namic’ (Ld ‘⁊ namige’). In A, ‘hine’ is written with the abbreviation ·N·.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 353, October 2026 (MS Cons); AU: corrected against Rabin p. 286 / 287, October 2026 (was “xiiii,”, now “XIIII,”); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 286 / 287, October 2026 (was “cxx:”, now “CXX:”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Burhbote</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">CXX: hundtweftigum A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">namie: and namige B</note>
